{"id":"resp_93360a212f49b554","created_at":1795617906,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_b5757b174f87898e","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shape(s) based on the requirement: The boundary between bottom and lower regions is taken where shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.\n\nWe have ontology terms: hullBoundaryPoint class, hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint object property from ship to hullBoundaryPoint, shellInclinationAngle property from benchmarkEntity to QuantityValue (QUDT), with unit DEG.\n\nWe also have termOwners: hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint owned by ship, shellInclinationAngle owned by hullBoundaryPoint.\n\nThus shape should target ship? Or target hullBoundaryPoint? Since requirement is about a point (boundary point) that belongs to a ship via the relationship. The shape likely needs to enforce that for each ship, there exists a hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint pointing to a hullBoundaryPoint that has a shellInclinationAngle value equal to 7 deg.\n\nWe cannot infer applicability beyond provided, but we have admission: focus_set mode COMPLETE_CLASS_POPULATION_PER_INPUT owner_class https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship. So target node is ship class. So shape targetClass ship.\n\nWithin ship shape, we need to enforce presence of hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint property (perhaps sh:minCount 1) linking to a hullBoundaryPoint with appropriate angle.\n\nWe need to use quantityEncoding numeric and unit predicates to encode quantity. Use sh:property with path to the quantity value.\n\nBut how to express that property? For the hullBoundaryPoint node, we need a shape that asserts that its shellInclinationAngle has value 7 deg.\n\nDefine a nested shape via sh:node of the property value (the object) maybe using sh:property with sh:node referencing another shape.\n\nThus two shapes: ShipShape and HullBoundaryPointShape.\n\nShipShape: targetClass ship; sh:property with path nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint; sh:minCount 1; sh:node :HullBoundaryPointShape.\n\nHullBoundaryPointShape: targetClass hullBoundaryPoint? Not necessary because used as node shape; it enforces presence of shellInclinationAngle property of type QuantityValue with numeric value 7 and unit DEG.\n\nFor quantity, we have QUDT model: shellInclinationAngle points to a QuantityValue (node). In that node, there should be qudt:numericValue 7 (xsd:decimal) and qudt:unit <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/DEG>. Use sh:property for both.\n\nAlso need to enforce that numeric value is exactly 7. Use sh:hasValue or sh:in? Since numeric literal 7. Use sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal.\n\nWe must use exact IRIs.\n\nDefine prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, xsd, qudt, nltl.\n\nMake sure to include the IRI for quantity class? Not needed.\n\nImplement shape.\n\nEdge cases: If multiple hasBottomRegion... okay.\n\nAlso need to record source text as rdfs:comment maybe using sh:message? Provide annotation referencing source.\n\nBut spec says preserve visible regulatory applicability text. Could include sh:description with source text.\n\nAdd sh:description with \"The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.\" (maybe include requirement id).\n\nWe shouldn't invent ownership beyond termOwners.\n\nThus shapes.\n\nNow produce Turtle with <BEGIN_SHACL> and <END_SHACL>. Ensure proper IRIs.\n\nPrefixes:\n\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n\nDefine shapes with node shapes.\n\nUse sh:NodeShape a sh:NodeShape.\n\nShipShape: :ShipBoundaryShape a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass nltl:ship; sh:description \"...\". Then property.\n\nHullBoundaryPointShape: :HullBoundaryPointShape a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass nltl:hullBoundaryPoint; sh:property for shellInclinationAngle with nested numeric.\n\nBut we may use sh:property for shellInclinationAngle, but we also need to check the QuantityValue's numeric and unit. That is two-level: hullBoundaryPoint has shellInclinationAngle linking to a QuantityValue node; that QuantityValue must have numericValue 7 and unit DEG.\n\nThus define shape for QuantityValue: :ShellInclinationAngleValueShape a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue; sh:property for qudt:numericValue with sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal; sh:property for qudt:unit with sh:hasValue unit:DEG.\n\nThen HullBoundaryPointShape property shellInclinationAngle with sh:node :ShellInclinationAngleValueShape and sh:minCount 1.\n\nThus we have three shapes.\n\nAdd comments referencing source: e.g., rdfs:seeAlso with requirement I2-005.\n\nNow produce final Turtle.\n\nCheck that we didn't use any undefined IRIs.\n\nAll good.\n\nNow output with markers.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_96afe688ff95c21e","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for ships – enforce that each ship has a bottom‑region boundary\n# point whose shell inclination angle is exactly 7 deg (requirement I2‑005,\n# clause I2.2.5).\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n:ShipBoundaryShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    rdfs:comment \"I2.2.5 – The boundary between the bottom and lower regions is to be taken at the point where the shell is inclined 7° from horizontal.\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node :HullBoundaryPointShape ;\n        sh:description \"Each ship must reference a hull‐boundary point that defines the bottom/lower‑region limit.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the hull‑boundary point – it must carry a shell inclination\n# angle quantity.\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n:HullBoundaryPointShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:hullBoundaryPoint ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shellInclinationAngle ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node :ShellInclinationAngleValueShape ;\n        sh:description \"The hull boundary point must have a shell inclination angle quantity.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape for the QUDT QuantityValue representing the shell inclination\n# angle – it must be 7 deg.\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------\n:ShellInclinationAngleValueShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:description \"Numeric value of the shell inclination angle must be 7.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:DEG ;\n        sh:class unit:DEG ;\n        sh:description \"Unit of the shell inclination angle must be degrees.\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":12976,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":12368,"input_tokens_per_turn":[12976],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":1767,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1152,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1767],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":14743},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}